{"entity": "SELF-RAG", "type": "concept", "description": "SELF-RAG is a model that enables arbitrary language models to generate text with reflection tokens by unifying them as next token predictions from an extended model vocabulary, incorporating both retrieval and reflection in its operations.<SEP>SELF-RAG is a framework developed to improve generative models by creating special tokens that allow self-evaluation and adapt during inference.</entity><SEP>A method for tailoring a language model without additional training, focusing on improving output based on retrieved passages and critic tokens.<SEP>A framework that enhances model performance for training and inference, demonstrating effectiveness in generating supported outputs and improving citation precision through a specified method of retrieval and parameter weighting.<SEP>SELF-RAG is a framework designed to enhance the quality and factuality of LLMs through retrieval on demand and self-reflection, enabling tailored model behaviors at test time using reflection tokens.<SEP>SELF-RAG is an analysis method that evaluates how model answers are generated based on retrieved passages or internal memory. It assesses the frequency of accurate answer generation across data segments."}
